List:

Mutable (you can change their content after creation)
Defined using square brackets: my_list = [1, 2, 3]
Can hold a mix of data types, e.g., my_list = [1, 'two', 3.0]

Tuples:

Immutable (once created, their content can't be changed)
Defined using parentheses: my_tuple = (1, 2, 3)
Can also hold a mix of data types, e.g., my_tuple = (1, 'two', 3.0)